id: pm-wfskfn
title: Register advanced retrieval as a search facet
description: "Make advanced retrieval a facet of the search noun rather than a second top-level command. The extension must register into the shared search contract, preserve search-advanced as a hidden alias, and emit one bounded migration hint with capability parity proof."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: cli-grammar,consolidation,search
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:07:35.264Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T06:18:01.673Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T06:18:00.931Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T06:18:00.931Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Advanced retrieval is reachable as a facet or subcommand of the search noun with identical capability; search-advanced keeps working as a hidden alias with a one-line migration hint; The package that provides advanced search registers into the search noun rather than claiming a second top-level name
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: The package registers search advanced with its stable SDK action and hidden legacy alias; shell completion discovers installed contributions and omits unavailable facets.
expected_result: "Advanced retrieval becomes a search facet while literal queries, package activation, flags, and legacy invocation remain supported."
actual_result: "Installed and absent-package completion, literal query escape, actual Bash/Fish/Zsh checks, npm/Bun consumers, and canonical/legacy contract regressions passed."
