comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T04:18:53.170Z","harness:codex","Design: package registers search advanced while retaining the search-advanced action identity and hidden compatibility spelling. Reuse the public namespace contracts and preserve core search queries, positional tokens, flags, and package activation rather than introducing a second search implementation."
  "2026-09-10T04:37:53.427Z","harness:codex","Integration evidence: installed bundled search and governance packages in an isolated tracker. New tests exposed namespace-parent registration ordering and negative-filter defaults entering package command validation. Canonical and legacy paths now share flag lookup; fixing these parser boundaries before acceptance. The focused namespace and history completion suite passed 35 tests; final acceptance and full gates remain pending."
  "2026-09-10T05:06:07.775Z","harness:codex","Manual shell verification found Fish quoting in nested suggestions and confirmed a discovery boundary to preserve: package facets must be suggested only when the package is active. Extending the public completion runtime configuration with installed namespace paths and wiring guide-shell registrations through it; retain static core aliases and shared SDK operation identities."
  "2026-09-10T05:37:55.715Z","harness:codex","Completion acceptance uses the real packaged CLI because the in-process test bridge can import a separate SDK registry instance. Production completion loads all installed command contributions and passes their canonical paths through public CompletionRuntimeConfig; package-absent leaves stay hidden. Bash completion acceptance passes absent and installed cases. Real Fish and Zsh syntax/runtime checks passed. Physical telemetry observation captured command_start and command_finish for canonical search advanced, preserving stable search-advanced operation identity."
  "2026-09-10T05:52:17.362Z","harness:codex","Verification relationship: installed search and guide-shell acceptance exercises the shared item/workspace namespace resolver, runtime package discovery, legacy command identity, and nested completion availability used by the sibling grammar delivery."
  "2026-09-10T06:18:00.173Z","harness:codex","Final verification: 660 test files and 8680 tests pass. Exact coverage is statements 63924/63924, branches 48623/48623, functions 13290/13290, lines 61268/61268. Source/export/member docstrings are 100 percent. TypeScript, ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, static structure, SDK/command/flag parity, refusal recovery, token budgets, graph composition, record integrity, credential scan, and linked tests passed. Manual temporary-project acceptance and packed npm/Bun/npx/bunx consumers passed. The independent public verifier confirms published 2026.9.9; this implementation is pending PR review and merge. GitHub currently has zero open PRs/issues and zero open dependency/code/secret alerts."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T06:06:47.259Z","harness:codex",Shell completion must discover installed command contributions beyond the completion provider itself. Test the actual CLI package boundary as well as the in-process SDK because separate module instances can carry separate registries. Preserve search -- advanced as a literal-query escape.
